# Dev Notes 51 — Runtime Capability Result/Event Envelope Integration v1

**Date:** 2026-06-19  
**Branch:** `runtime-capability-result-event-envelope-integration-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared contract-only result/event outcome scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted execute-action outcome smoke, existing execute-action/orchestration smokes, contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact/package guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed. No real-runtime test is required for the declared scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds one narrow, modular, contract-only result/event outcome seam after `runtime-capability-execute-action-orchestration-v1`.

The branch proves that an accepted execute-action orchestration descriptor can be paired with normalized Runtime Dev result envelopes and action events without starting execution.

Current descriptor chain before this branch:

```text
actionEnvelope
  -> capability bus action
  -> router route plan
  -> service plan
  -> backend adapter plan
  -> capability execution plan
  -> executor skeleton handoff descriptor
  -> backend adapter invocation descriptor
  -> execute-action orchestration descriptor
```

New branch output:

```text
accepted execute-action orchestration descriptor
  -> result/event outcome descriptor
```

The new descriptor is a bus-owned outcome contract artifact.

It does not execute actions, call services, call backend adapters, call `workerBridge`, import `llama_worker`, enqueue requests, stream tokens, load models, settle runtime requests, or touch lifecycle behavior.

---

## 2. Modular ownership

Ownership boundaries preserved:

```text
runtime/bus/executeAction/ owns execute-action composition/orchestration/outcome contracts.
runtime/execution/ owns capability execution and executor skeleton descriptors.
runtime/backends/ owns backend adapter and backend invocation descriptors.
runtime/router/ owns route validation and route/model/profile compatibility.
runtime/models/ owns model bundle metadata.
runtime/profiles/ owns hardware profile metadata.
runtime.mjs / workerBridge / llama_worker own real runtime/native behavior and remain untouched.
```

The outcome helper consumes existing orchestration, result envelope, action event, execution, and backend invocation validators instead of redefining those schemas.

This preserves the bus-owned outcome boundary without promoting backend invocation descriptors, executor skeleton descriptors, or orchestration descriptors into executable behavior.

